+/// Trusted CDP input on a standalone browser cannot preserve background
+/// posture: [`BrowserPlatform::standalone_trusted_input_background_limitation`]
+/// reports that the dispatch raises the standalone window. A bound record
+/// proves standalone-ness through its CDP window id — the pre-existing
+/// proof — or through its endpoint access class, which also covers standalone
+/// browsers bound without a Browser-domain window id: a tiling compositor or
+/// an endpoint that omits `Browser.getWindowForTarget` still owns a native
+/// window the dispatch would raise. Embedded Chromium endpoints keep the
+/// exact pre-existing cdp_window_id behavior. A driver-owned headless record
+/// (`windowless`) has no native window, so the limitation does not apply.
+pub(crate) fn standalone_trusted_input_limitation(
+    record: &super::store::TargetRecord,
+    platform_limitation: Option<&'static str>,
